what is the formal definition of Big-O?
- When we are talking T(n) = O(g(n))
--> g(n) is the upper bound of function T(n).
--> meaning that there exist c(scalar), n_0(a particular point), such that 
for all n when greater than n_0, 0 <= T(n) <= c*(g(n))


what is the formal definition of Big-omega?
- When we are talking T(n) = Ω(g(n))
--> g(n) is the lower bound of function T(n)
--> meaning that there exist c(scalar), n_0(a particular point), such that
for all n when greater than  n_0, 0 <= c*(g(n)) <= T(n)

what is the formal definition of Big-θ?
--> between big-omega and big-O
-->  c*(g(n)) <= T(n) <= c'*(g(n))